/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Mitigation Strategies To address these risks, organizations are implementing a variety of mitigation strategies. Developer training is a crucial element in mitigating AI-related risks, with 56% of respondents prioritizing this approach to ensure developers are equipped to handle the unique security challenges of AI-generated code. Code reviews and security testing, employed by 40%, also provide an essential layer of scrutiny, ensuring that AI-generated code meets quality and security standards.)
/E (Mitigation Strategies To address these risks, organizations are implementing a variety of mitigation strategies. Developer training is a crucial element in mitigating AI-related risks, with 56% of respondents prioritizing this approach to ensure developers are equipped to handle the unique security challenges of AI-generated code. Code reviews and security testing, employed by 40%, also provide an essential layer of scrutiny, ensuring that AI-generated code meets quality and security standards.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
2334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Governance frameworks were adopted by 26% of organizations to establish clear policies and procedures for managing AI-generated code. These frameworks can guide organizations in evaluating the risks associated with GenAI and enforcing security protocols. Specialized AI security tools, used by 37%, offer a targeted approach to addressing the unique vulnerabilities introduced by AI-driven processes.)
/E (Governance frameworks were adopted by 26% of organizations to establish clear policies and procedures for managing AI-generated code. These frameworks can guide organizations in evaluating the risks associated with GenAI and enforcing security protocols. Specialized AI security tools, used by 37%, offer a targeted approach to addressing the unique vulnerabilities introduced by AI-driven processes.)
